TEXT 64 96 Left 2 ;Parameter ioff:\nSwitching off at i<ioff
TEXT -248 88 Left 2 ;Switching off the circuit at high current momentan values\n( ioff=100A) a very high voltage spike.\nSwitching off at ioff=5A leads to no voltage spike\neine gewaltige Spannungserhöhung an der Spule\nSwitching off inductances should be done best at current zero
TEXT 64 8 Left 2 ;Hint to ioff:\nIf ioff is to small and the simulation timestep is to high\nswitching of may fail. If this occur increase ioff\nand/or make the minimal timestep smaller\nor use the breakpoint device
TEXT 176 192 Left 2 ;Frequency of the open circuit\nfrequency=1/2/pi/sqrt(L*C) =\n338Hz.
TEXT -256 168 Left 2 ;Spikes occur because the energy of the open\ncircuit cannot go immeadeately to zero\nIf the switching time is very short U have to be\nvery high so that U*I*dt = energy is decreased fast \nto a zero value.\nThrough the capacitance the energy can be \ndecrease slower. If C is not present the \nsituation is more severe (Test it with smaller values\nof C). At a real switcher the energy is burned in\nthe electric arc of the switcher and also the switcher\nis constructed to switch at current zero
